-- title:
--   Taylor–Wiles modules, strict ordinary non-flat case
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation ring with finite residue field $k$, $p\neq 2$ a prime lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$, and $\bar\rho$ a residual Galois representation over $k$ (a two-dimensional $k$-space with a $\mathrm{Gal}(\bar{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$-action factoring through a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$) which is absolutely irreducible. Let $S\supseteq S_{\min}\ni p$ be finsets of primes with, for $q\neq p$ prime, $q\in S_{\min}$ exactly when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$, and with $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ of characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$ for $\sigma$ in inertia at each $q\in S_{\min}\setminus\{p\}$. Let $N$ be squarefree with all prime divisors in $S$, divisible by every $q\in S_{\min}\setminus\{p\}$, with every prime divisor $\neq p$ in $S_{\min}$, and with $p\mid N$; assume `GaloisRep.IsFlatAt` fails for $\bar\rho$ at $p$. Let $r\geq 5$ be prime, $r\notin S$, $r\nmid Np$, $p\nmid r-1$, with $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\sigma)^2\neq (r+1)^2$ for every Frobenius $\sigma$ at every place above $r$, and assume weight-two cusp forms of level $\Gamma_0(N)$ are spanned over $\mathbb{C}$ by forms with integral $q$-expansion. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) to $k$ with $\det(X-\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_\ell))=X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$ for all primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, let $\mathbb{T}=$ [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) be the corresponding localisation, and let $H_n$ be a `HeckeGaloisRepDatum` for $(N,S,\mathcal{O},\theta)$ with ring $\mathbb{T}$ (a map $\pi$ from the Hecke algebra to $\mathbb{T}$ lifting $\theta$ and generating $\mathbb{T}$ over $\mathcal{O}$, an interpolation property for $\mathcal{O}$-valued characters, and a rank-two adic representation $H_n.\rho$ over $\mathbb{T}$ with Frobenius characteristic polynomials $X^2-\pi(T_\ell)X+\ell$ and absolutely irreducible residual representation). Let $L$ be a $\mathbb{T}$-module, finite and free over $\mathcal{O}$ in a compatible way, and suppose the Hecke operators at the auxiliary level commute ([`CuspForm.AuxLevel.OpComm N r S 𝒪`](def/CuspForm_AuxLevelHeckeModule.html#L30), hypothesis $hc$) and that $e_{ML}$ is an $\mathcal{O}$-linear isomorphism of $L$ with [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.ML N r S 𝒪 θ hc`](def/CuspForm_AuxLevelHeckeModule.html#L46), carrying the action of $\pi(T_\ell)$ for each generator $g$ at level $Nr$ to the action of the polynomial variable $X_g$. Then for every $t$, every injective $qv\colon \mathrm{Fin}\,t\to\mathbb{N}$ with each $qv_i$ prime, $qv_i\notin S$, $p\mid qv_i-1$, $qv_i\geq 5$, and $\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob})$ having two distinct eigenvalues at every place above $qv_i$; for all deformation ring data $D_{\min}$ for the minimal strict ordinary condition of level $S_{\min}$ and $D_Q$ for the strict ordinary condition of level $S_{\min}\cup\{qv_i\}$ together with unipotence on inertia at the $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$; for every local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\varphi\colon D_{\min}.R\to\mathbb{T}$ with $D_{\min}.\rho\otimes_\varphi\mathbb{T}\cong H_n.\rho$; and for all characters $cyc_q$ describing the Galois action on $q$-th roots of unity, surjections $\pi_\Delta$ from $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ onto $\Delta_i=\mathrm{Multiplicative}(\mathbb{Z}/p^{v_p(q-1)})$ for $q\neq p$, an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\varepsilon\colon D_Q.R\to D_{\min}.R$ which is local with $D_Q.\rho\otimes_\varepsilon D_{\min}.R\cong D_{\min}.\rho$, and $\iota\colon \mathcal{O}[\Delta_Q]\to D_Q.R$ with $\Delta_Q=\prod_i \mathrm{Multiplicative}(\mathbb{Z}/p^{v_p(qv_i-1)})$, such that $\varepsilon\circ\iota$ sends all group-like elements to $1$, $\ker\varepsilon$ is generated by the $\iota(g)-1$, and for each $i$ inertia at each place above $qv_i$ acts on some $D_Q.R$-basis of $D_Q.\rho.V$ diagonally through $\iota$ of $\pi_\Delta(cyc(\sigma))$ placed in the $i$-th coordinate and its inverse: there exists a module $M_n$ over $D_Q.R$, over $\mathcal{O}[\Delta_Q]$ and over $\mathcal{O}$ compatibly, which is nontrivial, finite over $\mathcal{O}$, free over $\mathcal{O}[\Delta_Q]$, whose $\mathcal{O}[\Delta_Q]$-action is the restriction of the $D_Q.R$-action along $\iota$, and an $\mathcal{O}$-linear isomorphism $e$ from the $\Delta_Q$-coinvariants $M_n/(\ker(\text{counit})\cdot M_n)$ onto $L$ satisfying $e(\overline{x\cdot m})=\varphi(\varepsilon x)\cdot e(\bar m)$ for all $x\in D_Q.R$.
--
--   This supplies the Taylor–Wiles modules $M_Q$ at the auxiliary level in the strict ordinary situation with $p\mid N$ and $\bar\rho$ not finite flat at $p$: free over $\mathcal{O}[\Delta_Q]$, semilinear over the deformation ring of the augmented problem, and with $\Delta_Q$-coinvariants identified with the given level-$N$ Hecke module $L$. It is the input consumed by the assembly step that combines level raising with the Taylor–Wiles patching argument.
